WEBVTT

00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:11.779
<v Grace Liu>Morning, everyone. Monday the 23rd of March. Have we got everyone on, or is Teams doing its Monday thing?</v>

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.509
<v Sarah Okafor>I'm here. Can hear you, Grace.</v>

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.730
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, here. Sorry, that clattering's my end.</v>

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:27.140
<v Hannah Price>Before we start properly, the charity bake sale on Friday was brilliant. Whoever did those brownies, honestly.</v>

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:32.030
<v Jamie Brennan>You mean the ones you hid behind the quality folders?</v>

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:40.119
<v Hannah Price>That was stock control. But yeah, the charity bake sale on Friday went really well. Just saying, not organising another one.</v>

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:45.840
<v Grace Liu>Good, because we're not turning this into a cake planning meeting.</v>

00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:53.439
<v Priya Raman>My weekend plans were mostly walking, until the weather got involved. Next weekend I'm thinking somewhere with a roof.</v>

00:00:54.049 --> 00:00:58.250
<v Fiona Doyle>Very sensible. March in Britain, bring all four seasons in a bag.</v>

00:00:59.799 --> 00:01:02.600
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, my waterproof apparently only works in theory.</v>

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:07.579
<v Grace Liu>Right, um, what's already cleared before we get onto the actual actions?</v>

00:01:09.609 --> 00:01:14.510
<v Jamie Brennan>I already swapped the filter on the GT2 Number 2 Bearing yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:01:16.579 --> 00:01:19.730
<v Grace Liu>Cheers, Jamie. Completed, then, not another one for today.</v>

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.930
<v Sarah Okafor>And I tested the line three yesterday and it's all fine now. That one's finished.</v>

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:38.390
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I saw the pressure on the line three dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own. Just passing on what I saw.</v>

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:45.700
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Mine was the completed test, yours is the brief dip. We're not adding another test off that.</v>

00:01:47.829 --> 00:01:55.530
<v Hannah Price>Similar sort of thing, I noticed the IM1 was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Just an observation.</v>

00:01:55.939 --> 00:01:59.790
<v Grace Liu>Understood. Settled down, no new action coming out of that here.</v>

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:08.550
<v Callum Reid>The other thing hasn't moved. I can't get to the line 3 chiller until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:14.189
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, that's still blocked. There's no access window to put against it.</v>

00:02:16.689 --> 00:02:22.289
<v Grace Liu>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Palletiser. That's the other outstanding blocker.</v>

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:26.030
<v Jamie Brennan>No confirmation my side either. Nothing definite on delivery.</v>

00:02:27.729 --> 00:02:31.930
<v Grace Liu>Okay. Both stay as blockers, not jobs we're pretending can happen today.</v>

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:38.710
<v Grace Liu>Fi, can you order spare parts for the line one next week? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:46.310
<v Fiona Doyle>Next week for placing the order, you mean, rather than saying they'll actually be here next week?</v>

00:02:48.449 --> 00:02:54.050
<v Grace Liu>Exactly, placing the order next week. No promise on arrival. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.219
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, I'll order spare parts for the line one next week.</v>

00:02:58.629 --> 00:03:02.830
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, talked over the start there. That was for Fi, not me?</v>

00:03:04.469 --> 00:03:06.569
<v Grace Liu>That's right, Fi owns that order.</v>

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:09.009
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, mine. All clear.</v>

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:18.860
<v Grace Liu>Priya Raman, can you write up the near miss at the boiler safety valve at half two? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:24.849
<v Priya Raman>Yeah. Just checking I heard you—at half two, not some time this afternoon?</v>

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:31.310
<v Grace Liu>At half two, yes. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:37.870
<v Priya Raman>Understood. I'll write up the near miss at the boiler safety valve at half two.</v>

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.280
<v Hannah Price>That's the write-up we're talking about, rather than another inspection?</v>

00:03:43.479 --> 00:03:46.979
<v Grace Liu>Just the write-up. I'm not adding an inspection to it.</v>

00:03:48.599 --> 00:03:52.800
<v Grace Liu>And I'll run the monthly fire alarm test this afternoon. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:58.759
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, someone started a pallet truck right beside me. Monthly test, normal priority?</v>

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.919
<v Grace Liu>Yep. I'll run it this afternoon, normal priority.</v>

00:04:03.439 --> 00:04:05.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Got you, Grace. The usual monthly test.</v>

00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:15.259
<v Grace Liu>Separate one: I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the IM1 hydraulic unit on the 3rd. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:04:15.879 --> 00:04:20.079
<v Sarah Okafor>On the 3rd, Grace? Just making sure I didn't hear 'at three'.</v>

00:04:21.339 --> 00:04:26.240
<v Grace Liu>On the 3rd. And yes, drop everything for that one. I'll take the sign-off.</v>

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:30.939
<v Priya Raman>Right, separate from my boiler safety valve write-up. Different urgency as well.</v>

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:38.050
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. Your write-up isn't an emergency; the IM1 hydraulic unit sign-off gets that top priority.</v>

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:44.860
<v Jamie Brennan>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the stretch wrapper. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:51.610
<v Grace Liu>Thanks, Jamie. You're taking the risk assessment update for the stretch wrapper, then?</v>

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:59.800
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll take it. The assessment update, not signing myself up for the work on the machine.</v>

00:05:00.519 --> 00:05:04.370
<v Hannah Price>Did we have a date against that? I didn't hear one.</v>

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:11.029
<v Grace Liu>No date stated for that one. Don't put an invented date against it.</v>

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:13.490
<v Fiona Doyle>Fine. Still top priority though, Jamie?</v>

00:05:15.279 --> 00:05:17.379
<v Jamie Brennan>Definitely. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:26.259
<v Callum Reid>And just so the blocked stuff doesn't disappear under all that, the line 3 chiller still has no production window.</v>

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.800
<v Grace Liu>Yep, still blocked. Same with the unconfirmed Palletiser delivery. No change to either.</v>

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:41.660
<v Jamie Brennan>And my filter swap stays in the done pile, please. Don't fancy getting credit for it twice and then being asked why it's not done.</v>

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:46.970
<v Sarah Okafor>Same for the line three test. Done yesterday, all fine now.</v>

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.980
<v Hannah Price>Very protective of the done pile this morning, aren't we?</v>

00:05:52.899 --> 00:05:55.350
<v Priya Raman>It's Monday. We've only just built it.</v>

00:05:57.389 --> 00:06:02.639
<v Grace Liu>Fair point. Right, the agreed actions are clear, and the blockers stay blocked. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:05.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, all.</v>
